245 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 80 0 R/E(GLP-1 \(Glucagon-Like Peptide-1\) is a hormone released in the gut after you eat. It acts as a messenger between your digestive system and your brain, helping regulate hunger, fullness, and blood sugar levels.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

246 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 80 0 R/E(When you consume a balanced meal, GLP-1 signals that nutrients are coming in and helps your body respond appropriately. It plays a key role in:)/Pg 15 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

247 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1534 0 R/E(Increasing feelings of fullness)/Pg 15 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

248 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1535 0 R/E(Supporting insulin release)/Pg 15 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

249 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1536 0 R/E(Slowing digestion)/Pg 15 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

250 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1537 0 R/E(Reducing appetite naturally)/Pg 15 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

251 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 80 0 R/T(INTRODUCTION TO GLP-1)/E(INTRODUCTION TO GLP-1)/Pg 15 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

252 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 80 0 R/E(In simple terms, GLP-1 helps your body recognize when it has had enough food, supporting fullness and stable blood sugar.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

253 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 80 0 R/T(Why GLP-1 Matters for Appetite & Weight Regulation)/E(Why GLP-1 Matters for Appetite & Weight Regulation)/Pg 15 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

254 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 80 0 R/E(Modern eating patterns \(fast meals, ultra-processed foods, constant snacking\) can disrupt natural satiety signals. When this happens, it becomes harder to feel satisfied, even when calorie intake is sufficient.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

255 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 80 0 R/E(GLP-1 helps restore that balance.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

256 0 obj
