273 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(One of GLP-1\220s most important roles is supporting blood sugar regulation. After a meal, GLP-1 stimulates insulin in a glucose, dependent way, meaning it activates when blood sugar rises and helps the body respond appropriately.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

274 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(At the same time, GLP-1 slows gastric emptying, or the rate at which food leaves the stomach. This creates a steadier release of glucose into the bloodstream, helping prevent sharp spikes followed by energy crashes.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

275 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(Stable blood sugar and stable appetite tend to work together. When glucose levels remain steady, cravings and impulsive eating often decrease naturally.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

276 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(When GLP-1 response is functioning well, the benefits often include:)/Pg 16 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

277 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(Fewer energy dips throughout the day)/Pg 16 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

278 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(Reduced \215sugar crashes\216)/Pg 16 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

279 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(Greater meal satisfaction)/Pg 16 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

280 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(More consistent hunger patterns)/Pg 16 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

281 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(Improved portion awareness and appetite control)/Pg 16 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

282 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(Benefits of a Strong GLP-1 Response)/Pg 16 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

283 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 81 0 R/T(Natural Support vs. Medication)/E(Natural Support vs. Medication)/Pg 16 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

284 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(GLP-1 medications have gained attention for their ability to enhance satiety and support weight management. These medications work by mimicking or amplifying the action of the GLP-1 hormone, helping regulate appetite and improve blood sugar control.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

285 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(However, the body naturally produces GLP-1 on its own. Nutrition and lifestyle habits play a meaningful role in how effectively this hormone is released and utilized, influencing satiety, insulin response, and overall metabolic balance.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

286 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(A food-first approach focuses on strengthening the body\220s natural signaling system through adequate protein intake, fiber-rich whole foods, gut-supportive nutrition, balanced meal structure, and slower, mindful eating habits. )/Pg 16 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

