1242 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 103 0 R/E(While food plays a major role in GLP-1 release, lifestyle habits also significantly influence how effectively this hormone functions. GLP-1 is part of a broader metabolic signaling system that responds to sleep, stress, movement, and daily rhythm.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

1243 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 103 0 R/E(When the body is chronically stressed, under-rested, or metabolically overloaded, appetite regulation becomes less predictable. Satiety cues may weaken, cravings can intensify, and blood sugar fluctuations may become more frequent. Supporting GLP-1 naturally requires creating an internal environment that feels stable, well-rested, physically active, and consistently regulated.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

