1288 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 105 0 R/E(Eating out while supporting natural GLP-1 function is manageable with simple, intentional choices. Focus on meals that prioritize protein, fiber, and blood sugar stability while limiting highly processed and rapidly absorbed foods.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

1289 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 105 0 R/T(1. Anchor Your Meal with Protein)/E(1. Anchor Your Meal with Protein)/Pg 40 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

1290 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 105 0 R/E(Choose dishes centered around grilled fish, chicken, lean meats, tofu, or legumes. Adequate protein enhances satiety signaling and helps regulate post-meal blood sugar.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

1291 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 105 0 R/T(2. Add Fiber-Rich Vegetables)/E(2. Add Fiber-Rich Vegetables)/Pg 40 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

1292 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 105 0 R/E(Build your plate around vegetables whenever possible. Ask for extra greens or swap refined sides for salads or steamed vegetables to improve fullness and digestion.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

1293 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 105 0 R/T(3. Choose Smart Carbohydrates)/E(3. Choose Smart Carbohydrates)/Pg 40 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

1294 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 105 0 R/E(If including carbohydrates, opt for whole-food options like beans, quinoa, or brown rice when available. Avoid large portions of refined breads, fries, or heavily processed grains that may spike blood sugar.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

1295 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 105 0 R/T(4. Keep Fats Balanced)/E(4. Keep Fats Balanced)/Pg 40 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

1296 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 105 0 R/E(Healthy fats like olive oil, avocado, or nuts can support satiety, but portion awareness matters. Avoid heavily fried or cream-based dishes that may slow digestion excessively.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

1297 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 105 0 R/E( Smart Ordering Rule)/Pg 40 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

1298 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 105 0 R/E(If menu descriptions include terms like crispy, battered, sweet, glazed, creamy, or loaded, the dish is likely higher in refined carbohydrates or excess fats. When in doubt, ask for sauces on the side, simplify the preparation, and prioritize grilled or baked options.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

1299 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 105 0 R/E(YOUR )/Pg 40 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

