1327 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 107 0 R/E(The strategies in this guide are designed to support the body\220s natural GLP-1 response through balanced nutrition and consistent lifestyle habits. They are not intended to diagnose, treat, or replace personalized medical care. Appetite regulation and metabolic health are influenced by factors such as medical history, medications, hormones, and overall lifestyle.)/Pg 42 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

1328 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 107 0 R/E(If you are taking GLP-1\205based medications or managing a condition like type 2 diabetes, consult your healthcare provider before making significant dietary changes. Adjustments to carbohydrate intake, meal timing, or physical activity may require monitoring to maintain stable blood sugar levels.)/Pg 42 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

1329 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 107 0 R/E(Those who are pregnant, breastfeeding, managing chronic conditions, or with a history of disordered eating should seek individualized guidance before following structured nutrition plans. Sustainable progress should support both physical and mental well-being.)/Pg 42 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

1330 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 107 0 R/E(GLP-1 function improves gradually through consistent habits, not extreme restriction. Prioritizing protein, fiber, sleep, stress management, and regular movement creates a strong foundation for long-term appetite regulation and metabolic balance.)/Pg 42 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

